Sir, please don't mock me.

244
00:12:40,473 --> 00:12:43,392
My oldest boy is in jail
for a crime he didn't do

245
00:12:43,517 --> 00:12:45,895
and Ethan here has terrible
health problems.

246
00:12:46,020 --> 00:12:47,480
Honey, you know I love you.

247
00:12:47,980 --> 00:12:49,857
And we're just making it
hand-to-mouth

248
00:12:49,982 --> 00:12:51,734
until this whole mess
is cleared up.

249
00:12:51,901 --> 00:12:54,153
And, and I have no idea
what you're talking about.

250
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:55,738
Really? Because these
Ferraris and Phantoms

251
00:12:55,863 --> 00:12:57,281
don't say
"hand-to-mouth" to me.

252
00:12:57,406 --> 00:12:59,366
It's like a master class
in dishonesty.

253
00:12:59,492 --> 00:13:01,911
You can't just bust in here
and accuse us of assassinations

254
00:13:02,286 --> 00:13:03,370
or whatever the hell else.

255
00:13:03,496 --> 00:13:04,997
- That's harassment.
- Yeah.

256
00:13:05,164 --> 00:13:07,416
- Where's your warrant?
- Ethan. Ethan, I, I understand.

257
00:13:07,541 --> 00:13:09,502
Being a Bittaker middle child
can't be easy

258
00:13:09,627 --> 00:13:11,337
and I, I sympathize

259
00:13:11,462 --> 00:13:14,340
but you really do have to take control
of these attention issues.

260
00:13:15,007 --> 00:13:17,635
Mrs. Bittaker, where have you
been for the last three days?

261
00:13:17,802 --> 00:13:18,844
Beauty shop.

262
00:13:19,261 --> 00:13:21,347
Oh, head shot! Sweet!

263
00:13:22,098 --> 00:13:23,641
Oh, check your left, Funguy.

264
00:13:23,766 --> 00:13:25,392
Left! Sniper's on you!

265
00:13:27,269 --> 00:13:29,855
Boom! Cal Da King
crushes again!

266
00:13:30,481 --> 00:13:32,358
- Kneel before me and die, scum!
- This is Caleb?

267
00:13:32,483 --> 00:13:33,526
He's the one
with the smarts, huh?

268
00:13:33,651 --> 00:13:35,069
This is a private office.
You gotta get out of here.

269
00:13:35,361 --> 00:13:37,071
What's that game he's playing?
It looks fun.

270
00:13:37,655 --> 00:13:38,697
- Come on.
- I'll go.

271
00:13:38,823 --> 00:13:40,116
- Get out of here!
- I'm going.

272
00:13:43,369 --> 00:13:44,411
Did you break her yet?

273
00:13:45,704 --> 00:13:46,997
Ah, okay. Let's go. Shall we?

274
00:13:47,123 --> 00:13:48,374
Pleasure meeting you,
Mrs. Bittaker.

275
00:13:48,499 --> 00:13:51,127
You have a wonderful family.
You must be very proud.

276
00:13:51,252 --> 00:13:52,878
You can sneer at me
all you like.

277
00:13:53,045 --> 00:13:54,255
I will. Thank you. Hey.

278
00:13:54,463 --> 00:13:57,216
Lay off the antidepressants.
They're making you slow.

279
00:13:58,425 --> 00:14:00,302
And you're still not happy,
are you?

280
00:14:10,896 --> 00:14:13,858
Don't ever make me
tell you this again.

281
00:14:14,024 --> 00:14:17,611
Do not play this game
when people are here.

282
00:14:17,820 --> 00:14:18,988
Got it?

283
00:14:26,996 --> 00:14:29,623
Here we are.
War Lord 3.

284
00:14:29,748 --> 00:14:31,250
Hold on.
"Cal Da King" you say.

285
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:33,252
I will run the logs.

286
00:14:35,087 --> 00:14:36,922
Yep. He's in a tournament circle.

287
00:14:37,047 --> 00:14:39,383
Caleb's gamer tag
is "Cal Da King."

288
00:14:39,550 --> 00:14:41,218
And from there
they can talk to anyone

289
00:14:41,343 --> 00:14:43,345
- anywhere, anytime?
- If they're in your circle.

290
00:14:43,721 --> 00:14:46,056
Well, bingo. That's how they
communicated with the hit man.

291
00:14:46,182 --> 00:14:47,224
Through the game.

292
00:14:47,349 --> 00:14:48,767
There's a thousand people
in Cal Da King's circle

293
00:14:48,934 --> 00:14:50,144
and conversations aren't logged.

294
00:14:50,269 --> 00:14:51,312
There's no way
to narrow it down.

295
00:14:51,437 --> 00:14:54,064
Is there some kind of
ranking, uh, thing?

296
00:14:54,190 --> 00:14:55,649
Of course.
That's the point.

297
00:14:55,816 --> 00:14:58,444
So if someone entered
the War Lord circle

298
00:14:58,611 --> 00:15:00,362
wo wasn't really there
as a gamer, then...?

299
00:15:00,487 --> 00:15:02,907
- They would suck, basically.
- Okay, let's run an ID trace

300
00:15:03,073 --> 00:15:06,285
on the bottom three
cyber warriors on that list.

301
00:15:06,410 --> 00:15:07,453
Of course.

302
00:15:10,164 --> 00:15:11,248
Just in time.

303
00:15:11,415 --> 00:15:13,167
Ballistics came up with a match.

304
00:15:13,292 --> 00:15:14,335
We have a suspect.

305
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:16,545
He has two previous hits
with the same make of bullet.

306
00:15:16,712 --> 00:15:17,755
Yeah, you were right, Jane.

307
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:19,089
This guy's definitely
from the region.

308
00:15:19,215 --> 00:15:20,257
Either that or he's been
operating here

309
00:15:20,382 --> 00:15:21,467
for the last few years.

310
00:15:21,592 --> 00:15:23,177
Downloads from
the realtor's smartphone

311
00:15:23,302 --> 00:15:24,929
says that he was meeting
someone named Lydon.

312
00:15:25,095 --> 00:15:26,764
Which is obviously an alias.

313
00:15:27,223 --> 00:15:29,058
Now the problem is we got
no fingerprints on this guy.

314
00:15:29,183 --> 00:15:31,310
Got no facial recognition,
no ID, nothing.

315
00:15:31,435 --> 00:15:33,520
Did we verify Lydon's
connection to the Bittakers?

316
00:15:33,646 --> 00:15:34,688
Not so far.

317
00:15:34,813 --> 00:15:37,107
Normally, with a guy like Lydon
there'll be a go-between involved.

318
00:15:37,483 --> 00:15:40,069
An intermediary who sidesteps
hard or cyber links.

319
00:15:40,653 --> 00:15:42,238
Now the problem is tracking it.

320
00:15:42,363 --> 00:15:44,573
There's too many potential
methods of communication.

321
00:15:44,698 --> 00:15:45,783
They could be using anything.

322
00:15:45,908 --> 00:15:48,369
They could be using dating sites
or a dead email address.

323
00:15:48,494 --> 00:15:51,622
Hell, they could even use
the old-school meet on the street.

324
00:15:51,747 --> 00:15:53,707
And we don't have time
to go through all of...

325
00:15:55,417 --> 00:15:56,460
Sorry to interrupt.

326
00:15:56,585 --> 00:15:57,711
Jane, I've got three names
for you.

327
00:15:58,420 --> 00:16:00,881
Ah, the Bittaker-Lydon connection.

328
00:16:01,340 --> 00:16:03,133
The bottom three are Juniesdad

329
00:16:03,259 --> 00:16:06,136
- 62-year-old male from Nova Scotia.
- Nah.

330
00:16:06,262 --> 00:16:09,640
OldGalsRule, 57-year-old
female from the UK.

331
00:16:10,182 --> 00:16:14,144
CountMeIn66, 35-year-old
female from Louisiana.

332
00:16:14,270 --> 00:16:16,605
- Her. Definitely her.
- Excuse me, Jane.

333
00:16:16,981 --> 00:16:18,023
What the hell
are you talking about?

334
00:16:18,148 --> 00:16:20,985
Well, I highly doubt your
go-between lives in Nova Scotia

335
00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:22,444
or the UK for that matter

336
00:16:22,611 --> 00:16:24,738
so I'm gonna vote on
Miss Louisiana.

337
00:16:25,864 --> 00:16:27,324
{\an8}"Hey, Wylie.
What've you got?"

338
00:16:27,449 --> 00:16:29,660
{\an8}"Her real name
is Peg Bailey from Lafitte"

339
00:16:29,785 --> 00:16:32,538
"and get this. Her ex used to work
as an enforcer for the Bittakers."

340
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:34,123
"Thanks, Wylie."

341
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:49,388
Looks pretty deserted.

342
00:16:49,888 --> 00:16:51,849
No, I think there's
someone here.

343
00:16:52,266 --> 00:16:54,310
We have to assume there is, okay?

344
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:55,728
All right, here's the plan.

345
00:16:56,228 --> 00:16:57,396
Lisbon and I are
gonna check it out.

346
00:16:57,563 --> 00:16:58,981
Jane, you stay.

347
00:16:59,106 --> 00:17:01,400
- Ken, really? Stay?
- Listen to me.

348
00:17:01,525 --> 00:17:03,569
For all we know, this lady's
just bad at video games

349
00:17:03,694 --> 00:17:06,030
all right? And I don't wanna
go upsetting the locals.

350
00:17:06,155 --> 00:17:08,907
Uh, I'm happy to wait here.
I'm not your dog.

351
00:17:11,285 --> 00:17:12,578
You jackass.

352
00:17:17,291 --> 00:17:18,334
Anybody here?

353
00:17:20,878 --> 00:17:22,379
Wait here.
I'll check around the back.

354
00:17:30,971 --> 00:17:33,474
Hey! Ho!
There's someone there.

355
00:17:41,565 --> 00:17:43,901
Excuse me, sir, does
Peg Bailey live here?

356
00:17:44,401 --> 00:17:46,528
Oh, uh, Peg's not here.

357
00:17:47,321 --> 00:17:50,157
We're with the FBI.
I'm Agent Lisbon.

358
00:17:50,324 --> 00:17:51,367
This is Patrick Jane.

359
00:17:52,284 --> 00:17:53,327
Who are you?

360
00:17:54,161 --> 00:17:56,246
Austin. You come a long way.

361
00:17:57,081 --> 00:18:00,042
Uh, hope it's nothing serious
that brought you down.

362
00:18:01,835 --> 00:18:05,214
I'm Peg's cousin Billy.
Wh, what's the issue, ma'am?

363
00:18:06,131 --> 00:18:07,299
Can we come in?

364
00:18:07,424 --> 00:18:09,802
It's a bit of a mess
but if you want.

365
00:18:10,719 --> 00:18:12,346
I can't say
when she'll be back.

366
00:18:13,931 --> 00:18:16,141
You can tell your friend
he can come in.

367
00:18:31,782 --> 00:18:33,617
Jane, stay with him.

368
00:18:33,909 --> 00:18:36,203
Okay. Spackman.

369
00:18:36,954 --> 00:18:38,705
Spackman? Look at me.

370
00:18:56,954 --> 00:18:58,872
- In, one, two.
- Spread it wide open.

371
00:18:58,997 --> 00:19:00,082
Out, one, two.

372
00:19:00,374 --> 00:19:02,668
Good job keeping his heart rate
down before we got here.

373
00:19:02,793 --> 00:19:03,836
Probably kept him
from bleeding out.

374
00:19:05,254 --> 00:19:06,588
Take care, Spackman.

375
00:19:07,631 --> 00:19:09,716
Hey, boss, they're bringing
Spackman to a hospital

376
00:19:09,842 --> 00:19:10,884
in Port Arthur now.

377
00:19:11,009 --> 00:19:12,177
But they have stabilized him.

378
00:19:12,344 --> 00:19:14,429
"I don't know. I think so.
He's gonna be okay."

379
00:19:14,555 --> 00:19:15,597
Uh, one more thing.

380
00:19:15,722 --> 00:19:18,225
We found a picture of Lily Stoppard
on Peg Bailey's computer.

381
00:19:18,600 --> 00:19:20,644
I want you two
to get back here ASAP.

382
00:19:20,769 --> 00:19:22,604
"We'll put you in a room
with a forensic sketch artist."

383
00:19:22,729 --> 00:19:24,064
All right, we'll get there
as soon as we can.

384
00:20:11,987 --> 00:20:13,864
Problem is, we got
too good a look at him.

385
00:20:13,989 --> 00:20:15,073
Well, how is that a problem?

386
00:20:15,198 --> 00:20:16,575
Well, this is who we saw.

387
00:20:18,452 --> 00:20:20,454
Lydon knows we got
a good clear look at his face.

388
00:20:20,621 --> 00:20:22,831
He, he'll never be that
good old boy again.

389
00:20:23,707 --> 00:20:24,917
Wylie, can you take this

390
00:20:25,042 --> 00:20:27,085
and generate
disguise variations on it?

391
00:20:27,252 --> 00:20:29,463
Hair length, glasses, beard,
that kind of thing?

392
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:31,423
- Yeah, sure.
- Thanks.

393
00:20:31,632 --> 00:20:33,175
So we'll see what that turns up.

394
00:20:41,224 --> 00:20:42,267
You wanted to see me, boss?

395
00:20:43,685 --> 00:20:46,188
- The arrogance of it all.
- Normally is.

396
00:20:46,939 --> 00:20:50,108
Witnesses, our people,
now this Peg Bailey?

397
00:20:50,984 --> 00:20:53,820
Jane figures they communicate
with her through video games.

398
00:20:54,529 --> 00:20:56,323
And just like that she's dead.

399
00:20:57,491 --> 00:20:58,992
God, I wanna crush
these people.

400
00:21:00,953 --> 00:21:03,080
Yeah? Me too.

401
00:21:05,540 --> 00:21:09,211
Ethan Bittaker has kidney
dialysis four times a day.

402
00:21:10,212 --> 00:21:12,130
I'm thinking he might be
a tad fragile

403
00:21:12,255 --> 00:21:14,341
with his health issues and all.

404
00:21:15,133 --> 00:21:17,469
And he has 38 months left
on his parole.

405
00:21:17,594 --> 00:21:18,637
You want me to lean on him?

406
00:21:21,723 --> 00:21:23,100
Let's both go lean on him.

407
00:21:24,142 --> 00:21:25,644
Let me go. Let me go. Mom!

408
00:21:25,769 --> 00:21:27,813
- What's going on? What are you doing?
- Stop it. Stop it. Mom.

409
00:21:27,938 --> 00:21:28,981
What's it look like we're doing?

410
00:21:29,106 --> 00:21:30,148
Well, it looks like you're arresting

411
00:21:30,273 --> 00:21:32,192
a dangerous parole violator,
Agent Cho.

412
00:21:32,359 --> 00:21:33,527
A parole violator?
What did I do?

413
00:21:33,860 --> 00:21:35,237
Consorting with a known felon.

414
00:21:35,529 --> 00:21:37,072
- Who?
- Kelvin Bittaker.

415
00:21:37,197 --> 00:21:38,949
- That's... That's my brother.
- That's ridiculous.

416
00:21:39,116 --> 00:21:40,242
Bad news, Ethan. Jail time

417
00:21:40,367 --> 00:21:41,410
- for the rest of your sentence.
- Mom. Mom.

418
00:21:41,535 --> 00:21:44,121
Wait, he has to be on dialysis
in less than an hour.

419
00:21:44,579 --> 00:21:47,165
Oh. Wow.
Well, that is a problem.

420
00:21:47,916 --> 00:21:49,334
Oh, well, how's this?

421
00:21:49,459 --> 00:21:51,044
We'll take his IV pole with us.

422
00:21:51,503 --> 00:21:53,130
Oh, just while we hold you.

423
00:21:53,255 --> 00:21:54,506
Now, I can't say
what's gonna happen

424
00:21:54,631 --> 00:21:56,508
- when he goes back to the pen.
- What's going on?

425
00:21:56,633 --> 00:21:58,301
Care to illuminate me, Agent?

426
00:21:58,468 --> 00:22:00,262
Supervising Agent Dennis Abbott.

427
00:22:01,054 --> 00:22:02,097
My.

428
00:22:02,264 --> 00:22:05,142
I'm gonna lay this out in words
that are designed to resonate.

429
00:22:06,059 --> 00:22:08,186
You're gonna call off
the hit on Lily Stoppard.

430
00:22:08,311 --> 00:22:11,481
You will call it off.
And you will deliver us Lydon.

431
00:22:11,898 --> 00:22:14,985
Or I won't be able to answer
to your son's well-being.

432
00:22:15,193 --> 00:22:17,612
I have no idea
what you're talking about.

433
00:22:17,988 --> 00:22:20,657
I'm truly lost
in this conversation.

434
00:22:20,949 --> 00:22:22,701
You wanna call my bluff?

435
00:22:23,410 --> 00:22:26,038
Well, do it. Please.

436
00:22:26,955 --> 00:22:29,875
Because while Ethan suffers,
or whatever happens to him

437
00:22:30,667 --> 00:22:33,420
it'll be on you.
He's nothing to me.

438
00:22:33,545 --> 00:22:36,298
But he's not, is he?
He's not nothing to you.

439
00:22:36,465 --> 00:22:38,925
You're a lawman
a supervising agent

440
00:22:39,051 --> 00:22:40,427
and he is a citizen.

441
00:22:40,802 --> 00:22:43,180
Sure, you may make him
unhappy or uncomfortable

442
00:22:43,305 --> 00:22:44,639
but you're not gonna
let him die.

443
00:22:44,765 --> 00:22:47,017
You're too damn ethical
for that.

444
00:22:49,603 --> 00:22:51,146
They don't know me,
do they, Cho?

445
00:22:51,313 --> 00:22:53,315
- No.
- I think I do.

446
00:22:53,523 --> 00:22:55,108
And I'm gonna bet
my son on it.

447
00:22:58,945 --> 00:23:00,530
Nice chatting with you, ma'am.

448
00:23:01,573 --> 00:23:03,200
Okay, go get that damn pole.

449
00:23:13,376 --> 00:23:17,881
One, two, three.
Bang, bang.

450
00:23:23,470 --> 00:23:25,972
I've set it for slideshow.
Let me know if you need more.

451
00:23:26,348 --> 00:23:28,308
- "Approaching Alpha..."
- Whoa, no. No, no, no, no, no.

452
00:23:28,433 --> 00:23:29,476
Hold on.

453
00:23:29,893 --> 00:23:31,144
Sorry. That's not it.

454
00:23:39,736 --> 00:23:40,779
Impressive.

455
00:23:42,697 --> 00:23:44,449
- Uh, can you print those out?
- Sure.

456
00:23:44,574 --> 00:23:46,701
And make sure you send them
to the hotel Lily's staying at

457
00:23:46,827 --> 00:23:47,869
as soon as you can.

458
00:23:48,829 --> 00:23:49,871
Nice job.

459
00:23:51,540 --> 00:23:53,083
Of course, Battlefield
was always my favorite

460
00:23:53,208 --> 00:23:55,377
- but that's just me.
- Battlefield?

461
00:23:56,044 --> 00:23:59,047
Oh. Yeah. You know,
the big boy game?

462
00:23:59,214 --> 00:24:01,007
But, hey, some people just can't
handle that kind of pressure.

463
00:24:01,133 --> 00:24:02,259
Oh, you mean that
little simple game

464
00:24:02,384 --> 00:24:04,052
with just a couple hotkeys
to worry about?

465
00:24:04,177 --> 00:24:05,303
Left trigger, right trigger, win.

466
00:24:05,762 --> 00:24:07,013
Oh, it won't be so simple

467
00:24:07,180 --> 00:24:09,307
when I no-scope you
for a team wipe.

468
00:24:09,432 --> 00:24:11,143
Listen, Vega, I think a little
1-V-1

469
00:24:11,268 --> 00:24:12,435
might clear this whole thing up.

470
00:24:12,561 --> 00:24:15,397
- Pistols only.
- Any day. Any time.

471
00:24:26,783 --> 00:24:27,993
The hit is still in play.

472
00:24:28,118 --> 00:24:29,703
We'll hold Ethan for 24 hours

473
00:24:29,828 --> 00:24:32,414
but Lydon has been a step
ahead of us the whole way.

474
00:24:32,789 --> 00:24:34,124
We have to get ahead now.

475
00:24:34,291 --> 00:24:36,001
Lily's testifying tomorrow.

476
00:24:36,376 --> 00:24:37,752
First thing in the morning, yeah.

477
00:24:37,961 --> 00:24:39,880
Well, Lydon probably already
scoped out her hotel

478
00:24:40,046 --> 00:24:41,131
so we'll change her.

479
00:24:41,256 --> 00:24:44,759
Uh, Lily's safe as long as she's
in her hotel room, yeah?

480
00:24:44,968 --> 00:24:48,138
Yes. She has full protection
from the car to the courthouse.

481
00:24:48,305 --> 00:24:49,598
But not en route to the car.

482
00:24:51,474 --> 00:24:52,684
- No.
- No.

483
00:24:52,809 --> 00:24:54,895
You... You wanna stay
ahead of Lydon?

484
00:24:55,145 --> 00:24:57,898
You leave Lily where she is.
We make our own plan.

485
00:24:58,648 --> 00:25:00,025
Okay, which is what?

486
00:25:01,109 --> 00:25:03,445
The general who chooses
the field of battle wisely

487
00:25:03,612 --> 00:25:05,530
wins before the fighting starts.

488
00:25:08,742 --> 00:25:10,994
Okay. I'm listening.

489
00:25:19,085 --> 00:25:22,464
"Lobbies are porous.
Multiple ways in and out."

490
00:25:22,631 --> 00:25:24,174
"Lots of camouflage too."

491
00:25:26,509 --> 00:25:27,802
"We'll need all hands on deck."

492
00:25:27,928 --> 00:25:30,764
"The moment we leave her room,
it's on."

493
00:25:32,349 --> 00:25:33,391
Bang.

494
00:25:35,185 --> 00:25:38,230
"Lydon will take advantage
of small spaces and passageways."

495
00:25:38,438 --> 00:25:41,566
"Areas not seen by the public.
He'll use it all."

496
00:25:43,693 --> 00:25:44,736
Bang.

497
00:25:47,530 --> 00:25:48,573
Bang.

498
00:25:49,824 --> 00:25:52,827
"We can't leave the husband behind.
We'll have to position him too."

499
00:25:53,954 --> 00:25:55,664
"He'll have an exit plan
well in place."

500
00:25:56,414 --> 00:25:57,832
"We're gonna want one too."

501
00:25:57,999 --> 00:25:59,167
- Bang.
- Bang.

502
00:25:59,334 --> 00:26:00,377
Bang.

503
00:26:01,086 --> 00:26:03,421
By my count,
I've been shot six times.

504
00:26:04,714 --> 00:26:06,466
Seven, but, uh...

505
00:26:08,218 --> 00:26:10,178
Okay, that's good.
I got it. Thank you.

506
00:26:38,206 --> 00:26:40,834
- Hi.
- You all right?

507
00:26:43,420 --> 00:26:45,630
Uh, yeah. I'm fine.

508
00:26:47,674 --> 00:26:50,677
Everything's gonna be okay tomorrow.
You know that, right?

509
00:26:52,262 --> 00:26:55,098
We know what we're doing.
It's a good plan.

510
00:26:55,932 --> 00:26:58,101
It's a really good plan.

511
00:26:58,935 --> 00:27:00,979
He has a good plan too.

512
00:27:01,855 --> 00:27:03,315
We're gonna be safe.

513
00:27:04,024 --> 00:27:05,734
Someone could get hurt.

514
00:27:07,610 --> 00:27:09,321
It's always dangerous.

515
00:27:11,614 --> 00:27:13,158
This is different.

516
00:27:14,993 --> 00:27:17,996
Everybody will be fine.
I promise.

517
00:27:18,997 --> 00:27:20,957
We're all gonna be fine

518
00:27:21,124 --> 00:27:23,543
if that's what this
insomnia is about.

519
00:27:25,295 --> 00:27:26,796
Yeah, you're right.

520
00:27:28,214 --> 00:27:30,925
I'm right
"everything's gonna be okay?"

521
00:27:32,093 --> 00:27:34,763
No, it's what
the insomnia's about.

522
00:27:35,805 --> 00:27:37,223
Come to bed.

523
00:27:38,683 --> 00:27:41,227
Please. Come on.

524
00:27:44,689 --> 00:27:45,815
All right.

525
00:27:51,237 --> 00:27:53,907
Do you want me to sing you
the lullaby

526
00:27:54,032 --> 00:27:56,368
I used to sing to my brothers
when they couldn't sleep?

527
00:27:59,454 --> 00:28:02,415
Um, I really, uh

528
00:28:03,708 --> 00:28:05,627
- don't wanna hear that.
- Okay.

529
00:28:07,879 --> 00:28:11,716
"Oh, we're halfway there"

530
00:28:12,133 --> 00:28:16,137
"Oh, livin' on a prayer"

531
00:28:16,304 --> 00:28:18,807
- "Take my hand and I'll..."
- Yeah.

532
00:28:19,015 --> 00:28:20,767
"Make it I swear"

533
00:28:20,892 --> 00:28:22,602
- Come on, sing.
- Oh, no.

534
00:28:22,727 --> 00:28:26,439
"Oh, livin' on a prayer"

535
00:28:26,564 --> 00:28:30,819
- "Take my hand and we'll make it, I swear"
- "Dear God, the pain"

536
00:29:46,976 --> 00:29:48,895
Wylie's in position
in the van outside.

537
00:29:49,020 --> 00:29:50,062
Okay, good.

538
00:29:50,188 --> 00:29:51,522
Everyone should be
getting into place soon.

539
00:29:51,647 --> 00:29:53,441
The only thing that we have
to do is run the timeline

540
00:29:53,566 --> 00:29:54,859
with Lily and Matthew.

541
00:29:55,151 --> 00:29:56,861
Uh, Vega, would you mind
getting them?

542
00:29:57,737 --> 00:29:59,614
Did you confirm that
the monitors are up in the van?

543
00:29:59,739 --> 00:30:02,450
Yes. Wylie was able to tap
into the hotel security system.

544
00:30:02,658 --> 00:30:04,660
All the monitors in the van
are on live feed now.

545
00:30:04,911 --> 00:30:06,245
Okay. Excellent.

546
00:30:06,913 --> 00:30:08,289
Hey, Lily.
How you doing?

547
00:30:08,706 --> 00:30:11,250
- Fine.
- That's good.

548
00:30:11,375 --> 00:30:12,502
Matthew, holding up?

549
00:30:13,127 --> 00:30:15,505
- Is it time already?
- No, not yet.

550
00:30:15,880 --> 00:30:17,965
Lily's, uh, expected to be
in the courthouse

551
00:30:18,132 --> 00:30:20,801
in a little under two hours,
so we'll leave in about an hour.

552
00:30:20,968 --> 00:30:22,428
Matthew, we're gonna need
to get you into position

553
00:30:22,553 --> 00:30:24,388
ahead of time before Lily
leaves the room.

554
00:30:24,514 --> 00:30:26,682
The car will be in the garage
of the hotel.

555
00:30:26,807 --> 00:30:28,351
The elevator goes directly
to them

556
00:30:28,476 --> 00:30:29,852
but we do have
alternative routes

557
00:30:29,977 --> 00:30:31,812
just in case
something happens.

558
00:30:33,356 --> 00:30:35,691
Can you people guarantee
that this will work?

559
00:30:36,192 --> 00:30:39,403
Today's plan has your wife's
safety as our only goal.

560
00:30:39,946 --> 00:30:41,989
We don't know exactly
how this is gonna play out

561
00:30:42,156 --> 00:30:45,326
but I can say that we've explored
every possible scenario

562
00:30:45,493 --> 00:30:46,619
and we're prepared for it.

563
00:30:47,745 --> 00:30:48,788
Well, thank you.

564
00:30:49,497 --> 00:30:50,623
All of you.

565
00:30:52,124 --> 00:30:53,543
Good. All right.

566
00:30:53,793 --> 00:30:54,919
Vega? If you don't mind.

567
00:31:00,508 --> 00:31:01,551
Hey.

568
00:31:02,510 --> 00:31:04,303
If anything happens to her
today, you know

569
00:31:04,428 --> 00:31:05,513
and I could have stopped it?

570
00:31:05,638 --> 00:31:08,474
Matthew. Your wife wants to do this.

571
00:31:08,599 --> 00:31:10,268
And we'll do everything
to keep her safe.

572
00:31:10,476 --> 00:31:11,811
It was a good decision.

573
00:31:13,062 --> 00:31:15,773
You need to trust her
on it, okay?

574
00:31:21,696 --> 00:31:23,656
I'd like to run through
the schematics one more time.

575
00:31:24,156 --> 00:31:26,993
I'm gonna take a...
Another quick look around.

576
00:31:27,118 --> 00:31:30,079
- I'll be back very soon.
- Okay.

577
00:31:32,415 --> 00:31:33,791
Okay, it's happening.

578
00:31:34,917 --> 00:31:36,586
- What's happening?
- Smoke in the hallway.

579
00:31:36,961 --> 00:31:38,212
- Smoke bomb?
- Yeah. Probably.

580
00:31:38,337 --> 00:31:40,089
It's okay.
Everybody just stay back, okay?

581
00:31:40,423 --> 00:31:41,465
All right?

582
00:31:41,591 --> 00:31:43,509
It's a decoy.
He wants the chaos.

583
00:31:43,634 --> 00:31:46,095
- We push on.
- Let's get into position.

584
00:31:46,220 --> 00:31:47,346
The elevators are gonna get
shut down.

585
00:31:47,513 --> 00:31:48,723
They do that in emergencies.

586
00:31:49,265 --> 00:31:52,018
Okay, Jane, I need you to get
down to the van where Wylie is.

587
00:31:52,268 --> 00:31:54,353
All right? Take the stairs.
Everybody, let's go.

588
00:32:00,026 --> 00:32:02,236
Make your way to the exits.
This is an emergency.

589
00:32:02,361 --> 00:32:04,155
You cannot go back to your room.

590
00:32:04,322 --> 00:32:05,906
Make your way to the exits.

591
00:32:06,032 --> 00:32:08,159
Everyone calm down.
Slow down. Take your time.

592
00:32:08,326 --> 00:32:09,577
This is an emergency.

593
00:32:09,785 --> 00:32:11,370
You cannot go back to your room.

594
00:32:11,704 --> 00:32:12,913
Make your way to the exit.

595
00:32:36,604 --> 00:32:38,939
Abbott and Magath are in
Lily's suite on monitor one.

596
00:32:39,482 --> 00:32:40,775
All right.
So how do I talk to them?

597
00:32:42,109 --> 00:32:44,654
Thank you. Abbott, it's Jane,
I'm in the van.

598
00:32:45,196 --> 00:32:46,238
"All right, copy that."

599
00:32:46,364 --> 00:32:48,407
"Lisbon and Cho are
in the bedroom with Lily."

600
00:32:48,658 --> 00:32:50,117
Good. So everyone's
accounted for.

601
00:32:50,242 --> 00:32:52,620
- Where's Vega?
- "I'm here. I'm in position."

602
00:32:52,745 --> 00:32:54,288
Excellent. Everyone listen up.

603
00:32:54,455 --> 00:32:57,291
Watch for emergency personnel.
Anyone in a uniform.

604
00:32:57,416 --> 00:32:58,793
That's how Lydon's coming in.

605
00:33:00,294 --> 00:33:01,921
"I left it up in my room.
I can't..."

606
00:33:19,249 --> 00:33:21,462
"Make your way to the exit.
We are evacuating the building."

607
00:33:21,588 --> 00:33:22,672
"Yeah, I left it up."

608
00:33:22,797 --> 00:33:25,883
Make your way to the exit.
We are evacuating the building.

609
00:33:26,050 --> 00:33:28,469
Stay calm. Everyone, everyone stay calm.
We are evacuating the building.

610
00:33:40,481 --> 00:33:41,524
"Are you okay?"

611
00:33:41,983 --> 00:33:43,443
Uh, you need to go now.

612
00:33:44,277 --> 00:33:45,820
"Copy that.
We're moving out."

613
00:33:46,713 --> 00:33:47,880
Are you good?

614
00:33:48,047 --> 00:33:49,590
- I'm good.
- Let's go.

615
00:33:49,966 --> 00:33:51,008
"This way."

616
00:34:17,118 --> 00:34:18,494
Oh, what do we have here?

617
00:34:18,619 --> 00:34:20,371
Is that him? Is that him?

618
00:34:20,496 --> 00:34:21,539
"Hey, Lisbon."

619
00:34:21,664 --> 00:34:23,082
"West stairwell
entering the 6th floor."

620
00:34:23,207 --> 00:34:25,126
"Could be him dressed as an EMT."

621
00:34:25,293 --> 00:34:26,794
- I got it.
- Uh, don't get too close.

622
00:34:26,919 --> 00:34:28,671
Just try to confirm if it's him.

623
00:34:28,796 --> 00:34:29,839
Jane, I got it.

624
00:34:45,480 --> 00:34:47,732
Jane, I'm on the sixth floor now.

625
00:34:47,982 --> 00:34:51,068
Yeah. Lisbon, it looks like he...
He may be at the other end.

626
00:34:51,194 --> 00:34:52,236
"Keep going."

627
00:35:04,957 --> 00:35:06,209
Ma'am, you okay?

628
00:35:06,542 --> 00:35:08,920
No, I, I, I hurt my ankle.

629
00:35:10,505 --> 00:35:12,089
- Which one is it?
- This one.

630
00:35:14,342 --> 00:35:16,427
All right, we're gonna need you
to reach out here, okay?

631
00:35:17,136 --> 00:35:18,596
You're gonna be okay.
Follow me.

632
00:35:19,222 --> 00:35:20,473
"Jane, it's not him."

633
00:35:26,854 --> 00:35:28,064
We're headed down
to the seventh floor.

634
00:35:35,404 --> 00:35:36,823
Abbott, by no means
rushing you

635
00:35:36,948 --> 00:35:39,075
but if things get tight,
we may have to rethink things.

636
00:35:39,283 --> 00:35:40,576
Good to know
you're not rushing me.

637
00:36:13,276 --> 00:36:14,443
Jane. The lights went out.

638
00:36:14,569 --> 00:36:16,779
Yeah, I, uh, I saw that.

639
00:36:16,904 --> 00:36:18,573
He is there. Be careful.

640
00:36:31,460 --> 00:36:34,297
Help! Help me!
I've been shot!

641
00:36:35,006 --> 00:36:36,215
- I got this.
- You got it?

642
00:36:36,340 --> 00:36:38,759
- All right. I got it.
- There's a shooter in the hotel.

643
00:36:39,969 --> 00:36:42,138
- He went downstairs.
- Okay, buddy. Hold on.

644
00:36:42,388 --> 00:36:44,682
Oh... oh, tell them to be careful.

645
00:36:44,807 --> 00:36:47,018
All right. Let me see
where you got hit.

646
00:36:56,736 --> 00:36:59,238
- Elevator's in locked-down.
- All right, try the stairway.

647
00:37:07,079 --> 00:37:08,122
Down!

648
00:37:22,386 --> 00:37:23,804
Suspect is down.

649
00:37:26,599 --> 00:37:28,935
We got an agent down,
service stairwell, seventh floor.

650
00:37:31,729 --> 00:37:32,855
"Everyone all right?"

651
00:37:32,980 --> 00:37:35,566
Jane. That's confirmed.

652
00:37:35,775 --> 00:37:38,235
The target's secure.
Great work team.

653
00:37:38,361 --> 00:37:39,445
"Did you get that, Lisbon?"

654
00:37:41,614 --> 00:37:43,074
Lisbon, where are you?

655
00:37:43,783 --> 00:37:45,451
Yeah. I got it. I'm here.

656
00:37:45,576 --> 00:37:47,036
I'm just getting back
with the team.

657
00:37:47,578 --> 00:37:48,788
It's good news.

658
00:38:01,759 --> 00:38:04,553
Well, here we are. Cozy.

659
00:38:05,096 --> 00:38:06,681
Lily Stoppard
took the stand today

660
00:38:06,931 --> 00:38:08,557
testified against your son Kelvin.

661
00:38:09,141 --> 00:38:10,685
We had a positive ID on Lydon

662
00:38:10,810 --> 00:38:12,728
hard evidence against you
and your family

663
00:38:13,020 --> 00:38:15,314
for five murders
and two attempted murders.

664
00:38:16,565 --> 00:38:18,401
So now you want me
to crack?

665
00:38:18,567 --> 00:38:21,487
Throw a child of mine
under the bus to save myself?

666
00:38:21,821 --> 00:38:24,448
- No.
- Good. Because I won't.

667
00:38:24,907 --> 00:38:27,201
Someone like you doesn't have
the faintest idea

668
00:38:27,326 --> 00:38:29,495
about the love a parent
has for a child.

669
00:38:29,620 --> 00:38:31,038
You're right. I don't.

670
00:38:32,123 --> 00:38:34,709
But I'm guessing it's what Jamie
Owen's mom felt about him.

671
00:38:35,292 --> 00:38:37,420
And the other five victims.
They had parents too.

672
00:38:38,295 --> 00:38:40,506
No deals. No bargaining.

673
00:38:40,965 --> 00:38:43,342
You're all gonna go down together.
It'll be a family trip.

674
00:38:46,512 --> 00:38:48,222
Have you figured it out yet, Belinda?

675
00:38:49,181 --> 00:38:51,892
How your never-miss hitman
missed so badly?

676
00:38:53,144 --> 00:38:54,854
"But he was close too."

677
00:38:56,022 --> 00:38:57,106
"But we knew that."

678
00:38:57,773 --> 00:39:00,484
"That's why we moved Lily
out of harm's way"

679
00:39:00,693 --> 00:39:02,111
"and subbed in one of our own"

680
00:39:02,528 --> 00:39:03,863
right before his eyes.

681
00:39:05,573 --> 00:39:09,076
Sometimes people just see
what they want to see.

682
00:39:11,662 --> 00:39:13,372
I don't mean to gloat, but...

683
00:39:21,714 --> 00:39:22,882
"Number of people remaining"

684
00:39:23,007 --> 00:39:26,010
"in the benefits roll
after drawing conditions week"

685
00:39:26,177 --> 00:39:28,554
"again shot up
by a hundred and eleven..."

686
00:39:28,679 --> 00:39:29,722
Hey, Vega.

687
00:39:29,847 --> 00:39:31,390
- You see this?
- What?

688
00:39:34,477 --> 00:39:36,771
Oh, oh, sorry, sorry.
Not this.

689
00:39:37,688 --> 00:39:38,731
I meant...

690
00:39:42,985 --> 00:39:44,236
No way.

691
00:39:45,071 --> 00:39:47,490
- Oh, it is so on.
- Oh, yeah?

692
00:39:47,615 --> 00:39:48,657
- Oh, yeah.
- You think?

693
00:39:48,783 --> 00:39:49,825
Psh. I know.

694
00:39:51,077 --> 00:39:52,578
- You are going down!
- Uh-uh.

695
00:39:52,953 --> 00:39:55,414
- Stop! Ha!
- Won't happen.

696
00:39:56,290 --> 00:39:58,250
- Hey, that's cheating!
- It's not.

697
00:39:58,918 --> 00:40:00,377
- I am so going for you.
- It's not gonna happen.

698
00:40:00,503 --> 00:40:01,962
- You are going down.
- You're gonna lose.

699
00:40:02,630 --> 00:40:04,131
You ready? Ready?

700
00:40:14,433 --> 00:40:15,559
There you are.

701
00:40:16,477 --> 00:40:18,354
- Here I am.
- Yeah.

702
00:40:21,982 --> 00:40:25,361
Uh, okay.
Uh, what's wrong?

703
00:40:26,529 --> 00:40:28,989
Why? You must already know.

704
00:40:31,659 --> 00:40:34,453
- Yeah. I, I took you...
- You took me off.

705
00:40:34,620 --> 00:40:36,330
- Mm-hm.
- On purpose.

706
00:40:36,789 --> 00:40:38,499
You knew that wasn't Lydon
on the sixth floor.

707
00:40:38,624 --> 00:40:40,626
You had to have,
but you sent me there anyway.

708
00:40:40,751 --> 00:40:41,877
Yeah, that's right.

709
00:40:43,003 --> 00:40:45,506
- I wanted to protect you.
- Protect me?

710
00:40:45,714 --> 00:40:47,675
- I'm an FBI agent. It's my job.
- Look, I know.

711
00:40:47,842 --> 00:40:49,593
And... And I'm sorry, but...

712
00:40:49,718 --> 00:40:52,012
But what?
You'd do it again?

713
00:40:54,807 --> 00:40:57,560
Yeah. I...
Yep. Probably would.

714
00:40:57,893 --> 00:40:59,270
- That's a problem.
- It's not a problem.

715
00:40:59,395 --> 00:41:00,604
- Oh, really? A big one.
- No...

716
00:41:00,771 --> 00:41:03,190
You can't do that. Okay,
you have to let me do my job.

717
00:41:03,357 --> 00:41:04,441
- If you can't...
- Yeah, I understand.

718
00:41:04,567 --> 00:41:06,694
If you can't... I don't know.

719
00:41:06,944 --> 00:41:08,404
Like... How do we work together?

720
00:41:12,116 --> 00:41:13,159
Well...

721
00:41:14,827 --> 00:41:16,412
We work it out.

